{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce statutory safeguarding checks for users of online dating platforms",
        "additional_details": "Millions now use dating apps to meet strangers, yet users may have little way of knowing whether someone has a serious history of sexual violence, domestic abuse, stalking or violence. People have been assaulted and killed after meeting through dating apps, and offenders can move between platforms. A government-run Dating Safety Check could add protection while keeping criminal-record data out of private companies' hands and preserving privacy, appeals and rehabilitation.",
        "background": "Introduce legislation requiring regulated dating apps to verify users\u2019 identities and participate in a government-administered Dating Safety Check for serious sexual, domestic abuse, stalking and violent offences, without giving dating companies access to users\u2019 criminal records.",
